Now I understand! The alias `setup.aliases.source_zenka_sid` includes `p7-log.append`. This means when ANY session sends `p7-log.append` to the cube, the cube prepends `SOURCE_ZENKA SOURCE_SID` to the args.

And in `base.handler.command`, the alias is looked up in `$data{'alias'}{$cmd}` (a global alias, not per-user).

Looking at the alias handling code in `base.handler.command` line 450-477:
```perl
# per user alias
$alias_to = $data{'user'}{$user}{'alias'}{$cmd}
    if exists $data{'user'}{$user}{'alias'}
    and exists $data{'user'}{$user}{'alias'}{$cmd};
my $cmd_orig  = $cmd;
my $args_orig = $call_args->{'args'};

##[ PROCESS \ ALIASES ]#######################################################

if ( defined $alias_to and length $alias_to ) {
    ...
}

## but also: ##
elsif ( exists $data{'alias'}{$cmd} ) {
    $alias_to = $data{'alias'}{$cmd};
    ...
}
```

Wait, I don't see the `elsif ( exists $data{'alias'}{$cmd} )` in the code I read earlier. Let me check more carefully.

Actually, looking at the code I read around line 450:
```perl
# per user alias
$alias_to = $data{'user'}{$user}{'alias'}{$cmd}
    if exists $data{'user'}{$user}{'alias'}
    and exists $data{'user'}{$user}{'alias'}{$cmd};
my $cmd_orig  = $cmd;
my $args_orig = $call_args->{'args'};

##[ PROCESS \ ALIASES ]#######################################################

if ( defined $alias_to and length $alias_to ) {
    ...
}
```

There's no `elsif` for global aliases. But wait, `base.init_code` sets `$data{'alias'}{$cmd}`. If the per-user alias isn't found, `$alias_to` is undefined. So the global alias wouldn't be applied!

Unless... `base.handler.command` checks global aliases somewhere else. Let me search.

